{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 18, :comments ["<b>And all the congregation they assembled on the first day of the second month.</b> On that very day on which the divine speech came to Moses, they assembled all the congregation and he began to count them, but the matter was not completed in a single day; therefore it was necessary to say ״ויפקדם במדבר סיני״ — that he completed their numbering in that place, not on that day. Thus wrote the Ramban, of blessed memory." "<b>And they declared their pedigrees.</b> They asked when they were born, for the reckoning of twenty years; or their genealogies were recorded and each one was traced to his tribe. Thus explained the sage Rabbi Abraham, of blessed memory."], :book :numbers, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 1, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:29:32.307693409Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}